INSERT INTO public."TestsData" ("TestId", "Questions", "Options", "Answers")
VALUES (490093200503015, ARRAY['"[8 marks] A practical problem in Cryptography and Network Security involves the syllabus topic need for security as applied within Security in Computing Environment. Explain how Need for Security applies, outline the steps and justify the result with an example."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] A practical problem in Cryptography and Network Security involves the syllabus topic terminologies used in cryptography as applied within Basics of Cryptography. Explain how Terminologies used in Cryptography applies, outline the steps and justify the result with an example."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] A practical problem in Cryptography and Network Security involves the syllabus topic block ciphers as applied within Symmetric Key Encryption. Explain how Block Ciphers applies, outline the steps and justify the result with an example."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] A practical problem in Cryptography and Network Security involves the syllabus topic integer factorization problems as applied within Public Key Encryption. Explain how Integer Factorization Problems applies, outline the steps and justify the result with an example."'::jsonb]::jsonb[], ARRAY[]::jsonb[], ARRAY['"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Need for Security appears in “Security in Computing Environment”. Define its role and features, relate it to Security Attack – Threats, Vulnerabilities, and Controls, Types of Threats (Attacks), provide a practical example and state one process/design check or limitation. Confirm the details against official teaching material.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to Security Attack – Threats, Vulnerabilities, and Controls, Types of Threats (Attacks), Security Services – Confidentiality. Include the relevant conditions, components, operating variables or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Cryptography and Network Security task and describe the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check against the stated objective and mention a limitation, error source or safety/design trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1. Confirm against official teaching material before use."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Terminologies used in Cryptography appears in “Basics of Cryptography”. Define its role and features, relate it to Substitution Techniques – The Caesar Cipher, One-Time Pads, The Vernam Cipher, Book Cipher, provide a practical example and state one process/design check or limitation. Confirm the details against official teaching material.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to Substitution Techniques – The Caesar Cipher, One-Time Pads, The Vernam Cipher, Book Cipher, Transposition Techniques – Encipherment/Decipherment Complexity. Include the relevant conditions, components, operating variables or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Cryptography and Network Security task and describe the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check against the stated objective and mention a limitation, error source or safety/design trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1. Confirm against official teaching material before use."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Block Ciphers appears in “Symmetric Key Encryption”. Define its role and features, relate it to Cipher Block Chaining Mode, Data Encryption Standard (DES) Algorithm – Overview of the DES Algorithm, Double and Triple DES – Double DES, Triple DES, provide a practical example and state one process/design check or limitation. Confirm the details against official teaching material.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to Cipher Block Chaining Mode, Data Encryption Standard (DES) Algorithm – Overview of the DES Algorithm, Double and Triple DES – Double DES, Triple DES, Security of the DES. Include the relevant conditions, components, operating variables or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Cryptography and Network Security task and describe the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check against the stated objective and mention a limitation, error source or safety/design trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1. Confirm against official teaching material before use."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Integer Factorization Problems appears in “Public Key Encryption”. Define its role and features, relate it to Characteristics of Public Key System, RSA Technique – Encryption-Method, Key Exchange, Diffie-Hellman Scheme, provide a practical example and state one process/design check or limitation. Confirm the details against official teaching material.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to Characteristics of Public Key System, RSA Technique – Encryption-Method, Key Exchange, Diffie-Hellman Scheme, ElGamal. Include the relevant conditions, components, operating variables or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Cryptography and Network Security task and describe the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check against the stated objective and mention a limitation, error source or safety/design trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1. Confirm against official teaching material before use."'::jsonb]::jsonb[]);

