VALUES (490093200511015, ARRAY['"[8 marks] A practical problem in Engineering Electromagnetics involves the syllabus topic cylindrical coordinate systems as applied within Vector Calculus and Coordinate Systems. Explain how Cylindrical coordinate systems applies, outline the steps and justify the result with an example."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] A practical problem in Engineering Electromagnetics involves the syllabus topic coulomb''s law as applied within Coulomb''s Law and Electric Field. Explain how Coulomb''s law applies, outline the steps and justify the result with an example."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] A practical problem in Engineering Electromagnetics involves the syllabus topic electric flux density as applied within Electric Flux Density and Gauss''s Law. Explain how Electric flux density applies, outline the steps and justify the result with an example."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] A practical problem in Engineering Electromagnetics involves the syllabus topic spherical coordinate systems as applied within Vector Calculus and Coordinate Systems. Explain how spherical coordinate systems applies, outline the steps and justify the result with an example."'::jsonb]::jsonb[], ARRAY[]::jsonb[], ARRAY['"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Cylindrical coordinate systems appears in “Vector Calculus and Coordinate Systems”. Define its role and features, relate it to spherical coordinate systems, gradient, divergence, curl, provide a practical example and state one process/design check or limitation. Confirm the details against official teaching material.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to spherical coordinate systems, gradient, divergence, curl, vector field interpretation. Include the relevant conditions, components, operating variables or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Engineering Electromagnetics task and describe the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check against the stated objective and mention a limitation, error source or safety/design trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1. Confirm against official teaching material before use."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Coulomb''s law appears in “Coulomb''s Law and Electric Field”. Define its role and features, relate it to electric field intensity, electric field due to charge distributions, line charge distribution, surface charge distribution, provide a practical example and state one process/design check or limitation. Confirm the details against official teaching material.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to electric field intensity, electric field due to charge distributions, line charge distribution, surface charge distribution, Coulomb''s Law and Electric Field. Include the relevant conditions, components, operating variables or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Engineering Electromagnetics task and describe the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check against the stated objective and mention a limitation, error source or safety/design trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1. Confirm against official teaching material before use."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Electric flux density appears in “Electric Flux Density and Gauss''s Law”. Define its role and features, relate it to Faraday experiment, relation between electric flux density and electric field, Gauss''s law, divergence theorem, provide a practical example and state one process/design check or limitation. Confirm the details against official teaching material.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to Faraday experiment, relation between electric flux density and electric field, Gauss''s law, divergence theorem, Maxwell first equation. Include the relevant conditions, components, operating variables or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Engineering Electromagnetics task and describe the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check against the stated objective and mention a limitation, error source or safety/design trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1. Confirm against official teaching material before use."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** spherical coordinate systems appears in “Vector Calculus and Coordinate Systems”. Define its role and features, relate it to Cylindrical coordinate systems, gradient, divergence, curl, provide a practical example and state one process/design check or limitation. Confirm the details against official teaching material.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to Cylindrical coordinate systems, gradient, divergence, curl, vector field interpretation. Include the relevant conditions, components, operating variables or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Engineering Electromagnetics task and describe the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check against the stated objective and mention a limitation, error source or safety/design trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1. Confirm against official teaching material before use."'::jsonb]::jsonb[]);

