INSERT INTO public."TestsData" ("TestId", "Questions", "Options", "Answers")
VALUES (4900932005050129, ARRAY['"[8 marks] A practical problem in Microcontroller and Interfacing involves the syllabus topic block diagram of microcontroller as applied within Introduction to Microcontroller. Explain how Block diagram of microcontroller applies, outline the steps and justify the result with an example."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] A practical problem in Microcontroller and Interfacing involves the syllabus topic interfacing of leds as applied within Interfacing with 8051 Microcontroller. Explain how Interfacing of LEDs applies, outline the steps and justify the result with an example."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] A practical problem in Microcontroller and Interfacing involves the syllabus topic temperature measurement using lm 35 temperature sensor as applied within Applications of 8051 Microcontroller. Explain how Temperature measurement using LM 35 temperature sensor applies, outline the steps and justify the result with an example."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] A practical problem in Microcontroller and Interfacing involves the syllabus topic features of microcontroller as applied within Introduction to Microcontroller. Explain how Features of microcontroller applies, outline the steps and justify the result with an example."'::jsonb]::jsonb[], ARRAY[]::jsonb[], ARRAY['"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Block diagram of microcontroller appears in “Introduction to Microcontroller”. Define its role and features, relate it to Features of microcontroller, Evolution of microcontroller, Difference between microprocessor and microcontroller, Microcontroller architecture- Von neuman and Harward architecture, provide a practical example and state one process/design check or limitation. Confirm the details against official teaching material.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to Features of microcontroller, Evolution of microcontroller, Difference between microprocessor and microcontroller, Microcontroller architecture- Von neuman and Harward architecture, RISC and CISC 2 8051 Microcontroller Architecture 05 Block diagram of 8051. Include the relevant conditions, components, operating variables or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Microcontroller and Interfacing task and describe the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check against the stated objective and mention a limitation, error source or safety/design trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1. Confirm against official teaching material before use."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Interfacing of LEDs appears in “Interfacing with 8051 Microcontroller”. Define its role and features, relate it to Segment display device, LCD display, DIP Switches, Push Button switches, provide a practical example and state one process/design check or limitation. Confirm the details against official teaching material.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to Segment display device, LCD display, DIP Switches, Push Button switches, Key denounce techniques. Include the relevant conditions, components, operating variables or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Microcontroller and Interfacing task and describe the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check against the stated objective and mention a limitation, error source or safety/design trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1. Confirm against official teaching material before use."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Temperature measurement using LM 35 temperature sensor appears in “Applications of 8051 Microcontroller”. Define its role and features, relate it to Battery voltage monitoring system, Developing Data Acquisition System for multiple channel inputs, GSM based application, Measurement of speed Total 42 hrs., provide a practical example and state one process/design check or limitation. Confirm the details against official teaching material.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to Battery voltage monitoring system, Developing Data Acquisition System for multiple channel inputs, GSM based application, Measurement of speed Total 42 hrs., Applications of 8051 Microcontroller. Include the relevant conditions, components, operating variables or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Microcontroller and Interfacing task and describe the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check against the stated objective and mention a limitation, error source or safety/design trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1. Confirm against official teaching material before use."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Features of microcontroller appears in “Introduction to Microcontroller”. Define its role and features, relate it to Block diagram of microcontroller, Evolution of microcontroller, Difference between microprocessor and microcontroller, Microcontroller architecture- Von neuman and Harward architecture, provide a practical example and state one process/design check or limitation. Confirm the details against official teaching material.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to Block diagram of microcontroller, Evolution of microcontroller, Difference between microprocessor and microcontroller, Microcontroller architecture- Von neuman and Harward architecture, RISC and CISC 2 8051 Microcontroller Architecture 05 Block diagram of 8051. Include the relevant conditions, components, operating variables or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Microcontroller and Interfacing task and describe the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check against the stated objective and mention a limitation, error source or safety/design trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1. Confirm against official teaching material before use."'::jsonb]::jsonb[]);

