VALUES (4900932005070129, ARRAY['"[8 marks] A practical problem in Network Routing and Switching involves the syllabus topic networking history as applied within Introduction to Networks. Explain how Networking history applies, outline the steps and justify the result with an example."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] A practical problem in Network Routing and Switching involves the syllabus topic ip address composition as applied within IP Addressing and Subnetting. Explain how IP address composition applies, outline the steps and justify the result with an example."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] A practical problem in Network Routing and Switching involves the syllabus topic cisco routers as applied within Routers, Switches and Cisco IOS. Explain how Cisco routers applies, outline the steps and justify the result with an example."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] A practical problem in Network Routing and Switching involves the syllabus topic ip routing as applied within IP Routing. Explain how IP routing applies, outline the steps and justify the result with an example."'::jsonb]::jsonb[], ARRAY[]::jsonb[], ARRAY['"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Networking history appears in “Introduction to Networks”. Define its role and features, relate it to types of networks, OSI reference model, TCP IP model, Ethernet technologies, provide a practical example and state one process/design check or limitation. Confirm the details against official teaching material.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to types of networks, OSI reference model, TCP IP model, Ethernet technologies, cabling. Include the relevant conditions, components, operating variables or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Network Routing and Switching task and describe the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check against the stated objective and mention a limitation, error source or safety/design trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1. Confirm against official teaching material before use."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** IP address composition appears in “IP Addressing and Subnetting”. Define its role and features, relate it to IP address types and classes, private IP addresses, public IP addresses, subnetting, provide a practical example and state one process/design check or limitation. Confirm the details against official teaching material.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to IP address types and classes, private IP addresses, public IP addresses, subnetting, variable length subnet masks VLSM. Include the relevant conditions, components, operating variables or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Network Routing and Switching task and describe the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check against the stated objective and mention a limitation, error source or safety/design trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1. Confirm against official teaching material before use."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Cisco routers appears in “Routers, Switches and Cisco IOS”. Define its role and features, relate it to switches, IOS and boot process, command line interface CLI, router basic configuration, provide a practical example and state one process/design check or limitation. Confirm the details against official teaching material.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to switches, IOS and boot process, command line interface CLI, router basic configuration, switch basic configuration. Include the relevant conditions, components, operating variables or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Network Routing and Switching task and describe the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check against the stated objective and mention a limitation, error source or safety/design trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1. Confirm against official teaching material before use."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** IP routing appears in “IP Routing”. Define its role and features, relate it to static routing, default routing, dynamic routing, administrative distance, provide a practical example and state one process/design check or limitation. Confirm the details against official teaching material.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to static routing, default routing, dynamic routing, administrative distance, routing metrics. Include the relevant conditions, components, operating variables or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Network Routing and Switching task and describe the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check against the stated objective and mention a limitation, error source or safety/design trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1. Confirm against official teaching material before use."'::jsonb]::jsonb[]);

