VALUES (4900932005090129, ARRAY['"[8 marks] A practical problem in Programming with Application Development (Android) involves the syllabus topic kotlin basics as applied within Kotlin Programming. Explain how Kotlin basics applies, outline the steps and justify the result with an example."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] A practical problem in Programming with Application Development (Android) involves the syllabus topic android sdk features as applied within Android and User Interface. Explain how Android SDK features applies, outline the steps and justify the result with an example."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] A practical problem in Programming with Application Development (Android) involves the syllabus topic files as applied within Android Storage. Explain how Files applies, outline the steps and justify the result with an example."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] A practical problem in Programming with Application Development (Android) involves the syllabus topic material design as applied within User Experience, Maps and Sensors. Explain how Material design applies, outline the steps and justify the result with an example."'::jsonb]::jsonb[], ARRAY[]::jsonb[], ARRAY['"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Kotlin basics appears in “Kotlin Programming”. Define its role and features, relate it to operations and priorities, decision making, loop control, collections and data structures, provide a practical example and state one process/design check or limitation. Confirm the details against official teaching material.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to operations and priorities, decision making, loop control, collections and data structures, functions. Include the relevant conditions, components, operating variables or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Programming with Application Development (Android) task and describe the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check against the stated objective and mention a limitation, error source or safety/design trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1. Confirm against official teaching material before use."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Android SDK features appears in “Android and User Interface”. Define its role and features, relate it to development tools, Android applications, application manifest, externalized resources, provide a practical example and state one process/design check or limitation. Confirm the details against official teaching material.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to development tools, Android applications, application manifest, externalized resources, application lifecycle. Include the relevant conditions, components, operating variables or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Programming with Application Development (Android) task and describe the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check against the stated objective and mention a limitation, error source or safety/design trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1. Confirm against official teaching material before use."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Files appears in “Android Storage”. Define its role and features, relate it to shared preferences, saving data, retrieving shared preferences, static resources, provide a practical example and state one process/design check or limitation. Confirm the details against official teaching material.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to shared preferences, saving data, retrieving shared preferences, static resources, file system. Include the relevant conditions, components, operating variables or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Programming with Application Development (Android) task and describe the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check against the stated objective and mention a limitation, error source or safety/design trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1. Confirm against official teaching material before use."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Material design appears in “User Experience, Maps and Sensors”. Define its role and features, relate it to RecyclerView, CardView, TabLayout, ViewPager, provide a practical example and state one process/design check or limitation. Confirm the details against official teaching material.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to RecyclerView, CardView, TabLayout, ViewPager, menus. Include the relevant conditions, components, operating variables or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Programming with Application Development (Android) task and describe the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check against the stated objective and mention a limitation, error source or safety/design trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1. Confirm against official teaching material before use."'::jsonb]::jsonb[]);

