VALUES (4900932005100129, ARRAY['"[8 marks] A practical problem in VLSI involves the syllabus topic historical perspective as applied within Introduction to VLSI Design. Explain how Historical perspective applies, outline the steps and justify the result with an example."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] A practical problem in VLSI involves the syllabus topic voltage transfer characteristics(vtc) of ideal inverter as applied within MOS Inverters 07 characteristics, MOSFET scaling, MOSFET capacitance. Explain how Voltage Transfer Characteristics(VTC) of Ideal inverter applies, outline the steps and justify the result with an example."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] A practical problem in VLSI involves the syllabus topic two input nand gate and nor gate with depletion nmos load as applied within Combinational MOS logic circuits. Explain how Two input NAND gate and NOR gate with depletion NMOS load applies, outline the steps and justify the result with an example."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] A practical problem in VLSI involves the syllabus topic cmos sr latch based on 2-input nor gates as applied within Sequential MOS logic circuits. Explain how CMOS SR latch based on 2-input NOR gates applies, outline the steps and justify the result with an example."'::jsonb]::jsonb[], ARRAY[]::jsonb[], ARRAY['"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Historical perspective appears in “Introduction to VLSI Design”. Define its role and features, relate it to VLSI design flow, Design Methodologies, Y- chart, Full custom design, provide a practical example and state one process/design check or limitation. Confirm the details against official teaching material.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to VLSI design flow, Design Methodologies, Y- chart, Full custom design, standard cell based design. Include the relevant conditions, components, operating variables or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete VLSI task and describe the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check against the stated objective and mention a limitation, error source or safety/design trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1. Confirm against official teaching material before use."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Voltage Transfer Characteristics(VTC) of Ideal inverter appears in “MOS Inverters 07 characteristics, MOSFET scaling, MOSFET capacitance”. Define its role and features, relate it to Typical VTC of a realistic n-MOS inverter, Noise Immunity and Noise Margins, Resistive load inverter and its analysis, Inverter with n-Type MOSFET load(Enhancement-Load NMOS Inverter and Depletion-Load NMOS Inverter), provide a practical example and state one process/design check or limitation. Confirm the details against official teaching material.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to Typical VTC of a realistic n-MOS inverter, Noise Immunity and Noise Margins, Resistive load inverter and its analysis, Inverter with n-Type MOSFET load(Enhancement-Load NMOS Inverter and Depletion-Load NMOS Inverter), CMOS Inverter. Include the relevant conditions, components, operating variables or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete VLSI task and describe the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check against the stated objective and mention a limitation, error source or safety/design trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1. Confirm against official teaching material before use."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Two input NAND gate and NOR gate with depletion NMOS load appears in “Combinational MOS logic circuits”. Define its role and features, relate it to CMOS logic circuits, CMOS NOR(2-input) and CMOS NAND(2-input) gate, Complex logic circuits, CMOS Transmission gates, provide a practical example and state one process/design check or limitation. Confirm the details against official teaching material.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to CMOS logic circuits, CMOS NOR(2-input) and CMOS NAND(2-input) gate, Complex logic circuits, CMOS Transmission gates, Combinational MOS logic circuits. Include the relevant conditions, components, operating variables or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete VLSI task and describe the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check against the stated objective and mention a limitation, error source or safety/design trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1. Confirm against official teaching material before use."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** CMOS SR latch based on 2-input NOR gates appears in “Sequential MOS logic circuits”. Define its role and features, relate it to CMOS SR latch based on 2-input NAND gates, Clocked SR latch, Clocked JK latch, JK Master-Slave flip-flops, provide a practical example and state one process/design check or limitation. Confirm the details against official teaching material.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to CMOS SR latch based on 2-input NAND gates, Clocked SR latch, Clocked JK latch, JK Master-Slave flip-flops, CMOS D-latch and edge triggered D-flip-flop. Include the relevant conditions, components, operating variables or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete VLSI task and describe the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check against the stated objective and mention a limitation, error source or safety/design trade-off.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1. Confirm against official teaching material before use."'::jsonb]::jsonb[]);
